      "english": "{0:There}, {2:having removed} {1:the cause of the initiating of desire-prompted and forbidden karma}, {4:in order to go on following} {3:the Lord's view}, {5:for the ascertainment of that cause}, {6:Arjuna} {7:said}, {8:‘now’} {9:— the verse's opening word}. {10:‘One who broods} {11:on the objects of sense}, {12:of a man}’ {13:and so on} {14:— by that, beginning so,} {15:before} {16:the root of misfortune} {17:was stated}. {18:Now} {19:and}, {20:‘of prakṛti}, {21:those bewildered by the guṇas’} {22:and so on} {23:— by that, beginning so,} {24:at great length} {25:it has been told}. {26:There}: {27:is it that} {28:all of them}, {29:even}, {31:are causes} {30:with equal primacy}? {32:Or else}: {34:is it that just} {33:one}, {35:the principal}, {36:cause}, {37:the others} {38:but} {40:merely} {39:co-operating with it}? {41:In that case} — {42:the first alternative} — {46:in the warding-off} {43:of all of them}, {44:severally}, {45:one by one}, {47:great} {48:would be the effort} {49:— that would follow}. {50:In the last alternative}, {51:but}, {52:with the one} {53:alone} {54:being removed}, {55:the accomplishing of one's task} {56:would follow} {57:— so Arjuna thinks}. {58:Hence}: {59:‘tell} {60:me}, {61:by what} {62:cause}, {63:impelled}, {64:driven}, {65:is this} {68:man}, {66:the one who does not follow your view}, {67:wholly bewildered of all knowledge} — {84:himself} {86:not wishing} {85:to do it}, {87:even} — {83:performing} {82:karma} {81:of many kinds}: {69:evil}, {70:entailing misfortune}, {71:altogether}, {72:wholly preceded by intent on the fruit}, {73:kāmya} — {74:such as the Citrā-rite and the rest}, {75:the means for slaying an enemy} — {76:and} {78:forbidden} — {77:such as the Śyena-rite and the rest}, {79:and} {80:the eating of kalañja and the rest} — {88:but not} {89:—} {90:the karma characterized by cessation}, {91:entailing the highest goal of man}, {92:taught by you}, {94:though wishing it}, {95:even} — {93:that karma} {96:does he do}? {97:For} {98:nor} {99:can dependence} {100:otherwise} {101:in this way} {102:be possible}.’ {103:Hence}: {104:‘the one by whom}, {105:as if by force}, {106:like} — {107:harnessed} {108:by a king}, {109:as} — {110:like a servant}, {113,114:though knowing, even}, {111:that it is opposed to your view} {112:and entails every misfortune}, {115:such} {116:karma} {117:performs} — {118:him}, {119:the one who sets me on the path of misfortune}, {120:me}, {121:regarding}, {122:tell it}, {123:having known him}, {124:for his complete extirpation}’ {125:— thus} {126:is the sense}. {127:By} {128:‘O Vārṣṇeya’} — {134:the vocative} — {140:he suggests}: {132:‘having descended} {131:by grace} {129:into the lineage of Vṛṣṇi}, {130:my maternal grandfather's family}’ {133:— so it is implied} — {135:the son of the Vṛṣṇi-woman} {136:am I}; {138:am to be regarded} {137:by you}’ {139:— so}.",
