      "locus": "3.37",
      "devanagari": "यस्तु बलवान् प्रवर्तकः स एष कामः। क्रोधोऽप्येष एव। तज्जन्यत्वात्। ‘कामात् क्रोधोऽभिजायते’ इति ह्युक्तम्। यत्रापि गुरुनिन्दादिनिमित्तः क्रोधस्तत्रापि भक्तिनिमित्ता निन्दा कामनिमित्त एव। ये त्वन्यथा वदन्ति ते सङ्करान्न सूक्ष्मं जानन्ति। उक्तं च — ‘ऋते कामं न कोपाद्या जायन्ते हि कथञ्चन’ इति। महाशनः। महद्धि कामभोग्यम्। महाब्रह्महत्यादिकारणत्वान्महापाप्मा। सर्वपुरुषार्थविरोधित्वाद्वैरी॥",
      "sanskrit": "yas tu balavān pravartakaḥ sa eṣa kāmaḥ | krodho 'py eṣa eva | taj-janyatvāt | 'kāmāt krodho 'bhijāyate' iti hy uktam | yatrāpi guru-nindādi-nimittaḥ krodhas tatrāpi bhakti-nimittā nindā kāma-nimitta eva | ye tv anyathā vadanti te saṅkarān na sūkṣmaṃ jānanti | uktaṃ ca — 'ṛte kāmaṃ na kopādyā jāyante hi kathañcana' iti | mahāśanaḥ | mahad dhi kāma-bhogyam | mahā-brahmahatyādi-kāraṇatvān mahā-pāpmā | sarva-puruṣārtha-virodhitvād vairī ||",
      "ourRendering": "What is the strong one, the instigator — that is this kāma. Anger too is just this same one, since it is born of it. ‘From kāma is born anger’ — so it runs, as indeed has been said. Wherever anger has for its occasion the reviling of a teacher and the like, there too, the reviling having devotion for its occasion, it is occasioned by kāma and by nothing else. Those who say otherwise — they, out of confusion, do not know the fine point. And it has been said: ‘Apart from kāma, anger and the rest do not arise at all, in any way whatever’ — so it runs. ‘The great devourer’: for great is what kāma has to enjoy. ‘The great evildoer’, because it is the cause of the great evils, the killing of a brahmin and the rest. The enemy, because it stands against every one of the ends a human life is for.",
      "source": "data/sources/sanskrit/vedanta/madhva_gita_bhasya.txt, adhyāya 3, ad 37",
