      "locus": "3.38",
      "devanagari": "कथं विरोधी सः? इदमनेनावृतम्। यथा धूमेनाग्निरावृतः प्रकाशरूपोऽप्यन्येषां सम्यगदर्शनाय तथा परमात्मा। यथाऽऽदर्शो मलेनावृतोऽन्याभिव्यक्तिहेतुर्न भवति तथाऽन्तःकरणं परमात्मादेर्व्यक्तिहेतुर्न भवति कामेनावृतम्। यथोल्बेनावृत्य बद्धो भवति गर्भस्तथा कामेन जीवः॥",
      "sanskrit": "kathaṃ virodhī saḥ? idam anenāvṛtam | yathā dhūmenāgnir āvṛtaḥ prakāśa-rūpo 'py anyeṣāṃ samyag-adarśanāya tathā paramātmā | yathādarśo malenāvṛto 'nyābhivyakti-hetur na bhavati tathāntaḥkaraṇaṃ paramātmāder vyakti-hetur na bhavati kāmenāvṛtam | yatholbenāvṛtya baddho bhavati garbhas tathā kāmena jīvaḥ ||",
      "ourRendering": "How is he an obstructer? This is covered by this. As fire is covered by smoke — though its own nature is light, even so — making for the failure to see it rightly on the part of others, so it is with the supreme self. As a mirror covered by dirt is not the cause by which other things are made manifest, so the antaḥkaraṇa, covered by kāma, is not the cause by which the supreme self and the rest are made manifest. As the embryo, having been covered by the caul, comes to be bound, so the jīva by kāma.",
      "source": "data/sources/sanskrit/vedanta/madhva_gita_bhasya.txt, adhyāya 3, ad 38",
      "textualNote": "The on-disk witness prints विरोधि (virodhi); the form required by the masculine saḥ is विरोधी (virodhī), and that is what is printed here.",
