      "english": "{0,1:And not} {2,3:of just anyone alone} {4,5:is this one an enemy} — {6,7:but rather} {8,9:of everyone} {10:— so it is}: {12:he states} {11:the illustration-bearing statement}, {13,14:in the word ‘dhūmena’.} {15:Of kāma}, {16:in non-denseness}, {17:in denseness}, {18,19:and in extreme denseness}, {20:respectively}, {21:are the illustrations.} {22,23,24:Even though covered by smoke}, {25:grimy}, {26:fire} {29,30:still does} {28:its own proper work}, {27:characterized by burning and the like.} {31,32:Covered by dirt}, {33:a mirror}, {34:however}, {38,39:does not do} {37:its own proper work}, {36:the catching of a reflection}, {35:because its quality of clarity is obstructed} — {40,41:though in its own form} {42:it is still perceived.} {43,44,45:Covered by the caul and the amnion}, {46:a fetus}, {47:however}, {50,51:does not do} {48:its own proper work}, {49:the stretching out of hands, feet and the like} — {52,53:nor} {54:in its own form} {55:is it perceived} {56:either.} {57:Thus}: {58:of kāma}, {59:in non-denseness}, {60:the recollection of the highest truth} {61,62:one is able to perform.} {63:In denseness}, {64,65:one is not able} {66:— so it is said.} {67,68:In denseness, however,} {72,73:this world} {69,70:would indeed be unconscious} {71:— so it would be} {74:altogether.}",
