      "english": "{2:Knowledge} {0:is covered} {1:by this} {4:perpetual enemy} {3:of the knower}: {6:for} {5:the knower} {7:knows} — {9:‘I} {11:have been set} {10:to what is not worth doing} {8:by this}, {12:before} {13:this very moment’} {14:— so he knows}. {16:And} {17:he is} {15:in pain} {18:always}, {19:without let}. {20:Hence} {21:that one} {23:is the perpetual enemy} {22:of the knower}, {24:not} {25:however} {26:of the fool}. {28:For} {27:he}, {33:seeing} {29:kāma} {32:as if} {31:a friend} {30:at the time of the craving}, {37:knows} only {36:when there has arrived} {35:the pain} {34:that is its effect}: {39:‘I} {41:have been brought} {40:to the state of being in pain} {38:by tṛṣṇā’} {42:— so he knows}, {43:not} {44:before} {45:that at all}. {46:Hence} {49:the perpetual enemy} {47:of the knower} {48:alone}. {50:In what form?} — {51:‘shaped as kāma’}: {52:kāma}, {53:that is, wanting}, {54:just that}, {55:is the form} {56:of it} {57:— so}, {58:‘shaped as kāma’}; {59:by that}. {60:‘Hard to fill’}: {62:the filling} {63:of it} {61:is done with pain} {64:— so}, {65:‘hard to fill’}; {66:by that}. {67:‘Never having enough’}: {68:there is not} {72:to be found} {70:any ‘enough’}, {71:any sufficiency}, {69:for it} {73:— so}, {74:analá}; {75:by that} {76:as well}.",
