      "english": "{3:Knowledge}, {1:though arisen} {0:from śāstra}, {2:even so}, {5:does not} {6:shine out} {4:for the direct seeing of the supreme self}, {8:covered} {7:by kāma}, {9:for the knower} {10:too}. {11,12:How much less} {13:for the little-knowing}? {14:‘Shaped as kāma’} — {15:that which goes by the name of kāma}, {16:the perpetual enemy}. {17:‘Hard to fill’}: {19:for} {20:kāma} {21:is filled} {18:with pain}. {23:For} {24:the rank of Indra and the rest} {22:is not} {26:got} {25:easily}. {27,28:Even if} {29:the rank of Indra and the rest} {30:has been reached}, {33:one wants} {31:again} {32:the rank of Brahmā and the rest} {34:— and so}, {37:there is} {36:no} {35:‘enough’-mind}: {38:hence} {39:analá}. {41:And} {40:it has been said}: {42:‘For knowledge} {44:and} {43:for Brahman} — {46:the smoke} {45:of fire}; {47:for buddhi} — {48:the dirt} {50:of a mirror}, {49:likewise}; {51:and then} {52:for the jīva} — {54:the caul} {53:of the embryo}: {55:such indeed} {56:is kāma’} {57:— so it runs}.",
