      "sanskrit": "adhitiṣṭhaty ebhir ayaṃ kāma ātmānam itīndriyāṇi mano buddhir asyādhiṣṭhānam; etair indriyamanobuddhibhiḥ kāmo 'dhiṣṭhānabhūtair viṣayapravaṇair dehinaṃ prakṛtisaṃsṛṣṭaṃ jñānam āvṛtya vimohayati — vividhaṃ mohayati, ātmajñānavimukhaṃ viṣayānubhavaparaṃ karotītyarthaḥ",
      "ourRendering": "This kāma takes its stand on the self by means of these — that is why the indriyas, manas and buddhi are its seat. kāma, by these — the indriyas, manas and buddhi, which have become its standing-place and which lean towards the objects of sense — having covered over knowledge, casts into delusion the embodied one, the one bound up with prakṛti: deludes him in many ways, makes him one who turns his face from the knowledge of the self and one whose whole bent is the experiencing of sense-objects — that is the sense.",
