      "sanskrit": "yasmāt sarvendriyavyāpāroparatirūpe jñānayoge pravṛttasyāyaṃ kāmarūpaḥ śatruḥ viṣayābhimukhyakaraṇena ātmani vaimukhyaṃ karoti, tasmāt prakṛtisaṃsṛṣṭatayendriyavyāpārapravaṇastvam ādau — mokṣopāyārambhasamaya eva, indriyavyāpārarūpe karmayoge indriyāṇi niyamya, enaṃ jñānavijñānanāśanam — ātmasvarūpaviṣayasya jñānasya tadvivekaviṣayasya ca nāśanaṃ pāpmānaṃ kāmarūpaṃ vairiṇaṃ prajahi — nāśaya",
      "ourRendering": "Because this enemy whose form is kāma works a turning-away from the self, by making one face the objects of sense, in the case of one who has set out upon the yoga of knowledge, which consists in the ceasing of all activity of the indriyas — therefore you, who lean towards the activity of the indriyas by being bound up with prakṛti, at the outset — at the very moment of beginning the means to liberation, just then — having reined in the indriyas within the yoga of karma, which consists in the activity of the indriyas, cast off — destroy — this one, ‘the destroyer of knowledge and of discernment’, the destroyer of the knowledge whose object is the self's own nature and of that whose object is the discriminating of it, the evil one, whose form is kāma, the enemy.",
