      "locus": "3.41",
      "sanskrit": "yasmād evam | yasmād indriyādhiṣṭhānaḥ kāmo dehinaṃ mohayati tasmāt tvam ādau mohanāt pūrvaṃ kāma-nirodhāt pūrvam iti vā | indriyāṇi śrotrādīni niyamya vaśīkṛtya | teṣu hi vaśīkṛteṣu mano-buddhyor api vaśīkaraṇaṃ sidhyati saṅkalpādhyavasāyayor bāhyendriya-pravṛtti-dvāraivānartha-hetutvāt | ata indriyāṇi mano buddhir iti pūrvaṃ pṛthaṅ-nirdiśyāpīhendriyāṇīty etāvad uktam | indriyatvena tayor api saṅgraho vā | he bharatarṣabha mahā-vaṃśa-prabhūtatvena samartho 'si | pāpmānaṃ sarva-pāpa-mūla-bhūtam enaṃ kāmaṃ vairiṇaṃ prajahihi parityaja hi sphuṭaṃ prajahi prakarṣeṇa mārayeti vā | jahi śatrum ity upasaṃhārāc ca | jñānaṃ śāstrācāryopadeśa-jaṃ parokṣaṃ vijñānam aparokṣaṃ tat-phalaṃ tayor jñāna-vijñānayoḥ śreyaḥ-prāpti-hetvor nāśanam",
      "ourRendering": "Since it is so — since kāma, whose stronghold is the indriyas, deludes the embodied one — therefore you, first: before the deluding, or, before the checking of kāma — restrain, bring under control the indriyas, hearing and the rest. For, these being brought under control, the bringing-under-control of manas and buddhi too is accomplished, since intending and determining are causes of misfortune only by way of the activity of the outer indriyas. Hence: previously, having designated separately ‘the indriyas’, ‘manas’, ‘buddhi’, here only ‘the indriyas’ has been said this much — or else: under the head of ‘indriya’, the inclusion of those two as well. O ‘bull among the Bharatas’ — by your being sprung from a great lineage, you are capable. ‘The evildoer’ — which has become the root of all evil — this kāma, the enemy — ‘renounce!’, give up; or, plainly, ‘strike down!’, kill decisively — or; ‘slay the enemy’, because of the conclusion's own words, and. ‘Jñāna’ — born of the teaching of scripture and teacher, indirect; ‘vijñāna’ — direct, its fruit: of those two, of knowledge and direct realization, which are the cause of attaining the highest good — ‘the destroyer’.",
