      "locus": "3.41",
      "sanskrit": "yasmād ayaṃ kāma-rūpo vairī nikhilendriya-vyāpāra-virati-rūpāyātma-jñānāyodyatasya viṣaya-rasa-pravaṇair indriyair jñānam āvṛṇoti tasmāt prakṛti-sṛṣṭa-dehādimāṃs tvam ādāv ātma-jñānodayāyārambha-kāla evendriyāṇi sarvāṇi tad-vyāpāra-rūpe niṣkāme karma-yoge niyamya pravaṇāni kṛtvā enaṃ pāpmānaṃ kāmaṃ śatruṃ prajahi vināśaya | hi yasmāj jñānasya śāstrīyasya dehādi-viviktātma-viṣayakasya vijñānasya ca tādṛg-ātmānubhavasya nāśanam āvarakam",
      "ourRendering": "Since this enemy, having the form of kāma, by means of the indriyas that are inclined toward the rasa of the sense-objects, covers over the knowledge — of one intent upon the knowledge of the self, whose very form is the cessation of the activity of all the indriyas — therefore you, possessing a body and the rest created by prakṛti, at the very outset, at the time of the beginning of the arising of the knowledge of the self: having reined in all the indriyas, having made them inclined toward the desireless yoga of karma, which has the form of their own activity, cast off — destroy — this evil one, kāma, the enemy. For — since it is the destroyer, the coverer, of the knowledge taught by scripture, whose object is the self as distinguished from the body and the rest, and of the discernment that is the direct experience of the self in just that way.",
