          "note": "The sharpest divergence in the passage. The same four words of the verse — yo buddheḥ paratas tu saḥ — are the ātman for Śaṅkara, the paramātman for Madhva, and here, for Rāmānuja, kāma itself: the enemy is ‘higher’ than buddhi in the plain sense that it can still move buddhi after buddhi has stopped."
