      "english": "{0,1:And not} {2,3:right at the start,} {4:for the conquest of manas and buddhi,} {5:should effort be made,} {6:because it is impossible} {7,8:— thus he says,} {9,10,11:in the words ‘the indriyas are higher’.} {12,13,14,15:Because of being hard to conquer even by heroes who are conquerors of the ten directions,} {16:by reason of excessive strength,} {17:they are best} {18,19:— that is the sense.} {20,21,22:Compared to the indriyas too,} {23:by reason of greater strength,} {24,25:manas is higher.} {26,27:Indeed, in dream,} {28,29,30:even though the indriyas have perished,} {31:because of its imperishability} {32,33:— that is the point.} {34,35,36:Compared to manas too,} {37,38:higher, more powerful,} {39:is buddhi,} {40:whose nature is discernment.} {41:In deep sleep,} {42,43,44:even though manas has perished,} {45,46,47:because of the imperishability of that buddhi's general form} {48,49:— that is the point.} {50,51,52,53:Compared to that buddhi too,} {54:further,} {55:by reason of an excess of strength,} {56,57:he who exists} — {58,59:even when that buddhi,} {60:through the practice of knowledge,} {61,62:has perished,} {63,64:he who shines forth} {65,66:— that is the sense.} {67,68:But he} {69:is the well-known} {70:jīvātman,} {71,72:the conqueror of kāma.} {73:Therefore,} {74:in reality,} {75,76:in every respect,} {77,78:by the exceedingly powerful jīvātman,} {80:having conquered} {79:the indriyas and the rest,} {81:kāma} {83,84:indeed can} {82:be conquered} {85:— so it is}: {86,87:here no} {88:incredulity} {89:is to be entertained} {90,91:— that is the point.}",
