      "locus": "3.43",
      "sanskrit": "upasaṃharati evam iti | buddher eva viṣayendriyādi-janyāḥ kāmādi-vikriyāḥ | ātmā tu nirvikāras tat-sākṣīty evaṃ buddheḥ paramātmānaṃ buddhvātmanaivaṃ tṛtayā niścayātmikayā buddhyātmānaṃ manaḥ saṃstabhya niścalaṃ kṛtvā kāma-rūpiṇaṃ śatruṃ jahi māraya | durāsadaṃ duḥkhenāsādanīyaṃ durvijñeyam ity arthaḥ",
      "ourRendering": "He sums up, thus ‘evam…’. The modifications beginning with kāma, born of objects, the indriyas and the rest, belong to buddhi alone. The self, however, is without modification, the witness of that so. Thus, having known the supreme self through buddhi, by that very self, thus, by that third [faculty], whose nature is determination, having steadied, by buddhi, oneself the manas, having made motionless, slay — kill! — the enemy in the form of kāma. ‘Hard to get at’ — to be reached only with difficulty, hard to know: that is, the sense.",
